            <ArticleTitle>The pharmacokinetics of a long-acting OROS hydromorphone formulation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137-44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1517/17425240903386658</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPORTANCE OF THE FIELD" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">New formulations of opiods can provide round-the-clock pain relief to improve pain management and quality of life for patients with chronic pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="AREAS COVERED IN THIS REVIEW" NlmCategory="METHODS">Information and comments on the pharmacokinetic processes associated with a new once-daily formulation of the potent opiod hydromorphone.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="WHAT THE READER WILL GAIN" NlmCategory="RESULTS">This review presents an overview of data from several small pharmacokinetic studies to gain a better perspective on the pharmacokinetic properties of a new long-acting formulation of hydromorphone.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="TAKE HOME MESSAGE" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The development of advanced oral formulation that deliver analgesic drugs over an extended period provides new solutions to improve pain management and quality of life for patients with chronic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
